This is one of the key highlights.

991
01:34:17,530 --> 01:34:21,190
要理解我们总能成长、学习，并追求更好的自己。
Understand we can always grow, learn, and strive for a better version of ourselves.

993
01:34:21,390 --> 01:34:22,610
这也是关键亮点之一。
This is one of the key highlights.

994
01:34:23,110 --> 01:34:25,810
有自负，我们就无法有效成长。
With an ego, we can’t grow as effectively.

995
01:34:25,810 --> 01:34:32,270
书中花了大量篇幅讨论这个话题。自负是人之常情。
And this is something the book spends a lot of time going over. Obviously, ego is a natural occurrence.

997
01:34:32,830 --> 01:34:37,050
但通过实用解决方案，你可以驯服它、控制它，从而做出更好决策。
But with practical solutions, you can tame it and control it to make better decisions.

999
01:34:37,210 --> 01:34:41,830
所以，重申，不是要消除自负。我们都有自负，必须与之共存。
So, again, it’s not about eradicating the ego. We’ve all got it. We have to live with it.

1000
01:34:41,970 --> 01:34:47,250
而是要理解它，以及它在我们内心最终扮演的角色——如何利用自负为我所用，而非被其所害。
But it’s about understanding it, and what role it ultimately plays within us—

1001
01:34:47,250 --> 01:34:52,530
how we can utilize the ego to our advantage rather than to our disadvantage.

1003
01:34:53,130 --> 01:34:58,030
最后，衡量表现时，别看结果，要看评分卡。
And then, lastly, to measure performance, not on outcome, but with a scorecard.

1005
01:34:58,330 --> 01:34:59,110
这部分见解很深刻。
This is quite insightful.

1006
01:35:00,110 --> 01:35:02,770
是本书很精彩的收官部分。
A great final section to the book.

1007
01:35:02,790 --> 01:35:03,730
强烈推荐这本书。
I highly recommend this book.

1008
01:35:04,110 --> 01:35:08,978
它的目的是激发你的思考，最终让你更好地理解自负可能在如何阻碍你。
Again, it is there to provoke your thought and ultimately give you a better understanding

1009
01:35:08,978 --> 01:35:12,547
of how your ego might ultimately be standing in the way.

1012
01:35:12,910 --> 01:35:14,170
好，那我们来总结一下。
All right. Let's go wrap up then.

1013
01:35:14,430 --> 01:35:16,290
第13单元的练习部分。
Unit 13 in the drill section.

1014
01:35:20,280 --> 01:35:22,340
现在进入练习环节。
This brings us now to our drill section.

1015
01:35:22,340 --> 01:35:25,580
这是第13单元的最后一张幻灯片。
This is the final slide of Unit 13.

1016
01:35:26,000 --> 01:35:26,860
你知道流程。
You know the drill.

1017
01:35:27,260 --> 01:35:28,360
去观看练习视频。
Go and watch the drill.

1018
01:35:28,700 --> 01:35:29,560
完成模板。
Complete the template.

1019
01:35:29,860 --> 01:35:35,380
对模板负责。观看指导教学练习。
Be accountable to that template. Watch the guided tuition drill.

1020
01:35:35,700 --> 01:35:37,780
做笔记。对比笔记。做调整。
Make some notes. Compare some notes. Make some adjustments.

1021
01:35:38,480 --> 01:35:43,540
回顾单元中讲解的视频，以及实操环节的视频。
Watch some of the videos we’ve dealt with during the units, and during the practical session.

1023
01:35:43,540 --> 01:35:46,219
确认无误后，进入第14单元。
Then, when you’re confident, move on to Unit 14.

1025
01:35:46,760 --> 01:35:50,460
在继续之前，先看看本杰明·富兰克林的一句名言：
Now, before we move on, a lovely little quote from Benjamin Franklin:

1027
01:35:52,120 --> 01:35:58,260
我们生来无知，但必须努力才能保持愚蠢。
We are all born ignorant, but one must work hard to remain stupid.

1029
01:35:59,300 --> 01:36:04,280
这是句很棒的话。我喜欢它的原因是，它真正强调了这个观点
It’s a fantastic quote. And why I like it is that it really pushes home this idea

1031
01:36:04,280 --> 01:36:06,947
我喜欢它的原因在于，它强调了一个观点：除非你拥有成长型思维，除非你愿意持续学习，从失败中成长，从尝试中进步——
that unless we have a growth mindset,

1032
01:36:06,947 --> 01:36:12,282
unless we’re willing to continuously be learning, growing through failures, through trying things—

1033
01:36:12,282 --> 01:36:17,617
unless we’re willing to do this, we’re going to forever remain ignorant.

1036
01:36:17,800 --> 01:36:21,880
否则你将永远停留在无知中。
So, in order to be that little bit less ignorant, you’re going to have to be willing to grow.

1038
01:36:22,540 --> 01:36:25,360
所以，要想少一点无知，你就得愿意成长。
Thank you, and I’ll see you again in Unit 14.
